  "conventions": {
    "durations_ms": "how long to hold each frame, same order as frames",
    "loop": "true = repeat forever; false = play once",
    "exit": "on a LOOPING state only: the one-shot to play when the condition holding it ends, e.g. purr -> purr_out. null means no settle exists and you should cut straight to rest. A looping state cannot use \"next\", so without this an exit animation would be unreachable from the manifest and you would have to infer it from its name.",
    "next": "animation to play when a non-looping one finishes. Every one-shot also ends on the resting pose, so a player that ignores this field still lands in a correct state.",
    "trigger": "when to play this. rest = default pose. fidget = pick at random by weight while resting. pet, pet_intense, reminder, held, nap, hungry, feed, stretch, drink, ready, dart, leap = driven by the named condition. none = reached only via another animation's next.",
    "weight": "relative likelihood among fidgets; absent otherwise",
    "props": "small sprites composited near him, each on its own canvas. registration is the point INSIDE the prop canvas that lands on the anchor; anchor is in his 50x50 coordinates, y downward from the top of that canvas. No motion is baked in - the app moves them. Fades are authored with alpha, so composite normally and do not ramp opacity.",
    "anchor_jitter": "suggested +/- scatter around the anchor, in his sprite pixels. A suggestion, not a rule.",
    "content_box": "union bounding box of non-transparent pixels across every frame. Use it only to answer \"will anything clip\" - it grows when any single animation reaches further than the rest pose, as alert_in does.",
    "rest_box": "bounding box of the REST POSE alone. Anchor to this, not content_box, so insets do not drift when an animation is added.",
    "baseline": "lowest opaque row of the REST POSE. His feet are planted in every animation except alert_in, which lifts him off the ground on purpose - baseline stays at the rest value and must not follow the hop.",
    "fidgets": "suggested random interval between fidgets, in ms.",
    "peek": "held poses for clinging to a screen edge; the app slides the window. edge_at is the canvas line the screen edge should sit on, and visible names the side that was composed to be seen. The far side exists only so a few extra pixels would not look amputated. flip_allowed is false: the tipped ear is on the visible side of peek_left, so a mirrored peek_right would show the wrong ear for as long as the peek lasts. look, inside each edge, is optional cursor tracking: single frames keyed \"dx,dy\" like directional.look, dy > 0 downward, \"0,0\" null meaning the loop frame 0. The whole eye is on screen in every variant.",
    "directional": "single frames the APP selects continuously, not timed animations. Key is \"dx,dy\", each in [-1,0,1], dx>0 to the viewer's right, dy>0 downward. look: \"0,0\" is the resting pose. ready_look: the same pupils on the ready crouch, \"0,0\" null meaning ready's frame 0."
  },
